<title>AUSTRALIA: ANZ reduces fixed home loan rates.</title>
<headline>ANZ reduces fixed home loan rates.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Australian and New Zealand Banking Group Ltd said on Thursday it had reduced interest rates on its one to five-year fixed rate owner-occupied and investment property loans.</p>
<p>The one-year fixed rate fell 0.50 percentage points to 6.45 percent.</p>
<p>ANZ's Australian retail general manager Peter Hawkins said the one-year fixed rate loan had no minimum overall term after 12 months and added the bank was committed to providing competitive home loans.  </p>
<p>ANZ's new fixed rates, which come into effect on July 21, are:</p>
<p>    1 year   6.45 percent (from 6.95 percent)</p>
<p>    2 year   6.99 percent (from 7.40 percent)</p>
<p>    3 year   7.25 percent (from 7.65 percent)</p>
<p>    4 year   7.75 percent (from 7.90 percent)</p>
<p>    5 year   7.85 percent (from 7.95 percent)</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
